{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q9MZ15","secondaryAccessions":["A0A4X1SP14","F1S2F6"],"uniProtkbId":"VDAC2_PIG","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2006-02-07","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2024-07-24","entryVersion":108,"sequenceVersion":2},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Sus scrofa","commonName":"Pig","taxonId":9823,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Laurasiatheria","Artiodactyla","Suina","Suidae","Sus"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q9Y5I6"}],"value":"Non-selective voltage-gated ion channel VDAC2"},"shortNames":[{"value":"VDAC-2"}]}},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q9Y5I6"}],"value":"VDAC2"}}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q60930"}],"value":"Non-selective voltage-gated ion channel that mediates the transport of anions and cations through the mitochondrion outer membrane and plasma membrane (By similarity). The channel adopts an open conformation at zero mV and a closed conformation at both positive and negative potentials (By similarity). There are two populations of channels; the main that functions in a lower open-state conductance with lower ion selectivity, that switch, in a voltage-dependent manner, from the open to a low-conducting 'closed' state and the other that has a normal ion selectivity in the typical high conductance, 'open' state (By similarity). Binds various lipids, including the sphingolipid ceramide, the phospholipid phosphatidylcholine, and the sterols cholesterol and oxysterol (By similarity). Binding of ceramide promotes the mitochondrial outer membrane permeabilization (MOMP) apoptotic pathway (By similarity). Associates with the translocase of the outer mitochondrial membrane (TOM) complex and PINK1 kinase at depolarized mitochondria, this interaction stabilizes PINK1 at the outer mitochondrial membrane and triggers downstream mitophagy by the recruitment of the E3 ubiquitin ligase PRKN (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}],"value":"Catalyzes the scrambling of phospholipids across the outer mitochondrial membrane; the mechanism is unrelated to channel activity and is capable of translocating both anionic and zwitterionic phospholipids"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"chloride(in) = chloride(out)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:29823"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:17996"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q60930"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"K(+)(in) = K(+)(out)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:29463"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29103"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q60930"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-L-serine(in) = a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-L-serine(out)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:38663"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:57262"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine(in) = a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine(out)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:38571"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:57643"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol)(in) = a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol)(out)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:38691"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:57880"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q60930"}],"value":"Monomer, homodimer and higher order oligomers; formation of higher order structures is necessary for scramblase activity (By similarity). Interacts with ARMC12 in a TBC1D21-dependent manner (By similarity). Interacts with KLC3 (By similarity). Interacts with SPATA33 (By similarity). Interacts with PPP3CC in a SPATA33-dependent manner (By similarity). As a homodimer, interacts with the TOM complex (By similarity). Upon mitochondrial depolarization, the TOM-VDAC assembly interacts with PINK1; the interaction stabilizes PINK1 at the outer mitochondrial membrane and triggers downstream mitophagy (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}],"value":"May localize to non-mitochondrial membranes"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}],"value":"Mitochondrion outer membrane","id":"SL-0172"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}],"value":"Multi-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9909"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}],"value":"Membrane","id":"SL-0162"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P21796"}],"value":"Consists mainly of a membrane-spanning beta-barrel formed by 19 beta-strands"}],"commentType":"DOMAIN"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}],"value":"Ubiquitinated by PRKN during mitophagy, leading to its degradation and enhancement of mitophagy. Deubiquitinated by USP30"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the eukaryotic mitochondrial porin family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Initiator methionine","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Removed","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}]},{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":2,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":294,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Non-selective voltage-gated ion channel VDAC2","featureId":"PRO_0000050507"},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":2,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":12,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Cytoplasmic","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}]},{"type":"Intramembrane","location":{"start":{"value":13,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":36,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helical","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":37,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":46,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Beta stranded","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}]},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":47,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":49,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Mitochondrial intermembrane","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":50,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":58,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Beta stranded","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P45880"}]},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":59,"modifier